  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENVIRONMENTAL WATER RESERVES: ENSURING HABITAT FOR MIGRATORY BIRDS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will: 1) protect 15.6 million acres of wetland habitat through the establishment of Presidentially decreed environmental water reserves that secure the flow of water necessary to maintain wetland habitat for migratory and resident birds; 2) develop the technical procedure to include the water needs of migratory birds as environmental indicators and implement a pilot application; 3) develop management plans incorporating this method for the two wetlands; and 4) train 25 local stakeholders to implement the management plans.</narrative>
  </description>
